      null,
      [
        "S004"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P027",
      "60 months\nfirst\nShaft seal leakage (normally less\nthan 0.5 mL/hour (~10 drops/hour) –\nI\nif more than 5 mL/hour shaft seal\nreplacement is recommended\nMotor ampere and/or power\nI\nconsumption within normal range\nUnusual noise\nI\nUnusual vibration (normally less\nthan 2.8 mm/s from pump itself –\nI\nand less than 7 mm/s incl. external\nexcited vibrations)\nPressure gauge readings to be\nwithin normal range (i.e. keep flow\nwithin 70 to 120% of BEP flow if\nI\nallowed by NPSHa <> NPSHr, see\nnote below)\nUnusual bearing temperatures\nI\n(normally less than 85°C)\nCheck (clean if required) drain hole\nI (M)\nfor shaft seal\nFor pump with bearing(s): Check\ngap between coupling and bearing\nI\nbracket/cover – to be at least 1 mm\n(see Section 10.3.8)\nPumps not running: Rotate pump\nshaft 2 to 3 revolutions or start\nM\nshortly (if pump is filled with liquid)\nRegrease pump and/or motor\nRefer to the following pages and motor manual (if motor bearings are rebearings\ngreaseable)\nSpacer coupling elastomer(s)\nI\nReplace mechanical shaft seal and\nM\nV-ring\nReplace pump bearings\nM\nReplace Spacer coupling\nM\nelastomer(s)\nNote: Operation outside 70 to 120 % of BEP flow reduce the pump life (incl. shaft seal and pump\nbearings) significantly.",
